      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Tested ACK d8e64d0\n\nBuilt and tested on Zen 2 (-O2). Passes `ctest` and valgrind ctime; on worst-case K=2323 the scan drops from 46.8s to 240ms (~195x). Factoring out `_scan_unlabeled_output` also cleanly isolates the $B_{spend} + t_k \\cdot G$ tweak for when #1914 lands.\n\nOne neat algebraic detail in `scan_target_batch`: `targets_gej[t]` starts at `unlabeled_output_ge` with $Z=1$, and `label_ge` is also affine. `gej_add_ge_var` pays for a generic 8M+3S step (multiplying by $Z_1=1$ four times), whereas an affine+affine to Jacobian addition has $Z_3 = X_2 - X_1$ and costs only 4M+2S.",
      "user": {
